Package: SIR
Title: Shape-Constrained Drug Synergy Testing via Isotonic Regression
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Amir", "Asiaee", , "amir.asiaeetaheri@vumc.org", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("James P.", "Long", role = "aut"),
    person("Samhita", "Pal", role = "aut"),
    person("Heather H.", "Pua", role = "aut"),
    person("Kevin R.", "Coombes", role = "aut"))
Description: A nonparametric framework for drug combination synergy
    testing. Interaction is defined as the deviation from a
    monotone-additive null fit by two-dimensional isotonic regression on
    a shared monotone surface. A degrees-of-freedom-corrected wild
    bootstrap yields calibrated p-values and effect summaries for each
    dose-response matrix, supporting principled hit calling and error
    rate control in large drug combination screens.
